1
00:00:00,413 --> 00:00:03,192
In this tutorial,
here's how to do the "stand walk".

2
00:00:03,776 --> 00:00:06,600
First, get on the unicycle as usual.

3
00:00:07,856 --> 00:00:12,936
Let's see how to place your feet
to get up into a "stand walk".

4
00:00:13,782 --> 00:00:17,594
Lift one foot and put
the arch of your foot

5
00:00:17,678 --> 00:00:24,093
on the frame and the front of it
on the tire to hold the unicycle still.

6
00:00:24,896 --> 00:00:27,947
Then slowly lift your other foot

7
00:00:28,138 --> 00:00:32,140
and put the front of it
on the other side of the frame.

8
00:00:33,563 --> 00:00:36,516
Once you're in position,
push with your legs

9
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,319
and push on the front of the saddle
to stand up,

10
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:44,805
keeping your body straight
to stay balanced on the unicycle.

11
00:00:45,456 --> 00:00:50,621
To move forward in a "stand walk",
you need your heel off the frame

12
00:00:50,705 --> 00:00:53,800
so you can push the tire and move.

13
00:00:58,189 --> 00:01:02,847
Once you know how to place your feet
and how to stand on the unicycle,

14
00:01:03,078 --> 00:01:06,695
you can practice along a wall,
riding across in a "stand walk"

15
00:01:06,779 --> 00:01:10,672
by pushing the tire with your foot
to move forward.

16
00:01:11,083 --> 00:01:14,140
Once you feel more comfortable,
try letting go of the wall

17
00:01:14,224 --> 00:01:19,687
little by little, until you've got
a perfect "stand walk" with no help.

18
00:01:20,903 --> 00:01:25,965
To start a "stand walk" without a wall,
begin with a "glide",

19
00:01:26,049 --> 00:01:30,442
then push to stand up,
like you did earlier with the wall.

20
00:01:30,579 --> 00:01:35,552
Then drive the wheel forward
by pushing with the foot on the tire.

21
00:01:35,876 --> 00:01:37,528
To get out of a "stand walk",

22
00:01:37,612 --> 00:01:40,880
you can switch to a "wheel walk"
or a "glide" first,

23
00:01:40,957 --> 00:01:44,234
then put your feet back on the pedals,
or go straight onto the pedals.

24
00:01:44,485 --> 00:01:46,886
Just make sure one pedal is at the bottom

25
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:50,260
so you can put your foot straight down
and ride off.

26
00:01:51,476 --> 00:01:52,920
Your turn!

27
00:01:53,004 --> 00:02:02,800
[Music]

